  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping Feasibility Coastal Protection Hoi An</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Many, almost all studies indicated that coastal protection in Vietnam is an expensive measure. So, until now, not many meaningful actions have been taken. However, a Dutch consortium has developed a concept that involves a revolving solution suitable for this situation. The consortium intends to present the idea during the visit of the Dutch prime minister to Vietnam in early April 2019. However, the Vietnamese government is unconvinced that such a solution would be applicable in Vietnam. The project aims to discuss and demonstrate to the Vietnamese government that coastal protection is feasible for Vietnam.</narrative>
  </description>
